The first operational lookup exposed a representation-order issue: K maps are commutative, but the generated lookup constructor rebuilds the active scope as `singleton(scope) ++ rest`. To match the fixed target’s nested map syntax, the writable total map union must choose the reverse association-list representative (`right ++ left`). I’m adding a regression test for that representation before changing the definition.
apply patch
