codex
The generated Base hides its executable map helpers behind Lean-private names, so ordinary `simp` cannot unfold them. I added a small proof-only tactic that resolves those existing private definitions by their generated names and unfolds them—no theorem or equation is introduced. This has closed the map lookup obligations without assuming any hook axiom. I’m now packaging the repetitive `Rewrites.tran` constructor plumbing so the operational trace remains auditable rather than becoming hundreds of manually instantiated metavariables.
