codex
The recursive inner-loop proof now closes using only ordinary rewrite constructors, including both divisibility outcomes and a well-founded integer measure. One representation issue surfaced for reuse inside the outer loop: the frozen target constructs the same local K map in two different key orders. I’m generalizing the proven trace over those two honest association-list layouts, so the proof does not assume an invalid structural equality between them.
